      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since a single soong module can contain combination of *.cpp and *.yy (or .c and .y) srcs, would we need to repeat the implementation/dynamic deps in this design? Vinh, do you know how we handled this repition for aidl? Do aidl modules allow combination of *.cpp and *.aidl files in srcs?\n\n\ne.g. the BUILD file in this design option will be\n```\n# system/tools/aidl/BUILD.bazel\ncc_library_static (\n  name \u003d \"libaidl-common\",\n  srcs \u003d [\n     \"logging.cpp\",\n     ...\n     # But not aidl_language_y.yy\n  ]\n  implementation_deps \u003d [ # Needs to be here since the parent module needs them\n     \"libbase\",\n     \"liblog\",\n     ...\n  ],\n  whole_static_deps \u003d [\n     \"libaidl-common_yacc\",\n  ],\n)\n\ncc_yacc_static_library (\n  name \u003d \"libaidl-common_yacc\",\n  src \u003d \"aidl_language_y.yy\",\n  implementation_deps \u003d [ # Needs to be repeated here too\n     \"libbase\",\n     \"liblog\",\n     ..., # Although some might not be necessary\n  ],\n )\n ```",
